1 NAME Donald Chester /Lufholm/
2 GIVN Donald Chester
2 _MARNM Lufholm
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 21 APR 1923
1 DEAT
2 DATE 4 JAN 1985
2 ADDR
3 STAE Minnesota
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth: 	Apr. 21, 1923 Minnesota, USA Death: 	Jan. 4, 1985 Minnesota, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT DONALD C. LUFHOLM 
2 CONT
2 CONT Duluth News Tribune & Herald, Jan 5, 1985 p. 6B
2 CONT
2 CONT Donald C. Lufholm, 61, of 1914 N. 51st Ave. E; died Friday in St. Mary's Hospital. He was a life-long Duluth resident. He had been employed as an installer for Western Electric Co. for more than 35 years, retiring in 1982. He was 
2 CONC a Navy Air Corps veteran of World War II, during which he spent much of his service in Saipan. He was a 1942 graduate of Denfeld High School. He was a member of Faith Lutheran Church and a former trustee. He was a life member of T
2 CONC elephone Pioneers of America and the Duluth Camera Club and was an honorary member of the Duluth Rose Society. He was known in recent years for his slide presentation, which was set to music, of the Duluth Rose Garden and of the r
2 CONC egion's wildflowers, entitled "Bloom Where You Are Planted." He is survived by his wife, Lois F.; a daughter Anine Lufholm of Duluth; his father and stepmother, H. Lawrence and Eldora Lufholm of Duluth; a brother, Charles of Dulut
2 CONC h; a sister Janet Carter of Artesia, CA; and a half-brother Peter Lufholm of Jackson, Miss. Visitatino will be at 4 p.m. Sunday in the Johnson Mortuary and from non to 1 p.m. Monday at Faith Lutheral Church, where services will be
2 CONC  at 1 p.m. Monday. Burial will be in Park Hill Cemetery.
