1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lena_Olin '''Lena Maria Jonna Olin'''] is a Swedish actress. She has been nominated for several acting awards, including a Golden Globe for The Unbearable Lightness of Being (1988) an
2 CONC d an Academy Award for Enemies, A Love Story (1989). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Other well-known films in which she has appeared include Chocolat (2000), directed by her husband Lasse Hallström, Queen of the Damned (2002), Casanova (2005) and The Reader (2008). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Olin was also a main cast member in the second season (and a recurring guest star in later seasons) of the television series Alias. Olin starred in the Swedish sitcom Welcome to Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Olin, the youngest of three children, was born in Stockholm, Sweden. An older brother died of cancer in 1960, 10 years old. She is the daughter of actress Britta Holmberg and director Stig Olin. She studied acting at Sweden's Nati
2 CONC onal Academy of Dramatic Art.[citation needed]
2 CONT
2 CONT In October 1974, at age 19, Olin was crowned Miss Scandinavia 1974 in Helsinki, Finland.
2 CONT
2 CONT From the mid 1970s through the end of the 1980s, Olin was for many years the partner of Swedish actor and Royal Dramatic Theatre colleague Örjan Ramberg. They had a son, Auguste Rahmberg (b. 1986). The relationship ended in the la
2 CONC te 1980s. She also had a brief relationship with Richard Gere, her co-star in Mr. Jones (1993 film), before marrying Lasse Hallström (see below) in 1994.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1992, Olin had met film director Lasse Hallström in Sweden. Two years later, in 1994, they married in Hedvig Eleonora Church in Stockholm. They have a daughter, Tora (born 1995). Olin lives in Bedford, New York with her husband
2 CONC  and children.
